+# Plan: DaemonSet Direct HostPath Mounts
+
+## Phase 1: Rework artifact-daemon to serve directories
+
+### [ ] Write tests for directory-based artifact serving
+- Test that `GET /artifacts/steps/<handle>/<name>` tars a directory on-the-fly and streams it.
+- Test that `DELETE /artifacts/steps/<handle>/` removes the entire step directory tree.
+- Test that `HEAD /artifacts/steps/<handle>/<name>` checks directory existence.
+- Test that GET on a missing directory returns 404.
+- File: `cmd/artifact-daemon/server_test.go`
+
+### [ ] Rework artifact-daemon HTTP server for directories
+- `GET /artifacts/steps/<handle>/<name>`: walk the directory, write tar stream to response (no pre-tarred file).
+- `DELETE /artifacts/steps/<handle>/`: `os.RemoveAll` on the step directory.
+- `HEAD /artifacts/steps/<handle>/<name>`: `os.Stat` on the directory.
+- `PUT /artifacts/steps/<handle>/<name>`: receive tar stream, extract to directory (for remote use cases).
+- Keep backward compatibility for flat tar files (Phase 1 of original track) during migration.
+- File: `cmd/artifact-daemon/server.go`
+
+### [ ] Update TTL sweeper to be build-aware
+- Sweeper scans `/steps/` only (not `/caches/`).
+- For each candidate directory, check if a pod with matching handle exists on this node.
+- Use K8s API (pod list filtered by node name + handle label) to determine active pods.
+- Only delete directories where: no matching pod + mtime > TTL.
+- Files: `cmd/artifact-daemon/sweeper.go`, `cmd/artifact-daemon/sweeper_test.go`
+
+## Phase 2: Direct hostPath output volumes
+
+### [ ] Write tests for hostPath output volume mounts
+- Test that when `ArtifactBackend=daemonset`, output volumes are hostPath subdirectories (not emptyDir).
+- Test that the hostPath is `/var/concourse/artifacts/steps/<handle>/<output-name>/`.
+- Test that the artifact-helper sidecar is NOT added in DaemonSet mode (no upload needed).
+- File: `atc/worker/jetbridge/daemonset_integration_test.go`
+
+### [ ] Implement hostPath output volumes in pod builder
+- In `buildVolumeMounts()`, when DaemonSet mode: create hostPath volumes for outputs instead of emptyDirs.
+- Path: `<ArtifactDaemonHostPath>/steps/<handle>/<output-name>/`.
+- HostPath type: `DirectoryOrCreate`.
+- Skip the artifact-helper sidecar entirely in DaemonSet mode (no upload phase).
+- Files: `atc/worker/jetbridge/container.go`
+
+### [ ] Remove upload phase for DaemonSet mode
+- `uploadOutputsToArtifactStore()`: no-op for DaemonSet mode (data is already on hostPath).
+- `uploadCachesToArtifactStore()`: no-op for DaemonSet mode (caches are direct mounts).
+- Still call `artifactLocator.Record()` with the pod's node name after step completion.
+- Files: `atc/worker/jetbridge/process.go`
+
+## Phase 3: Local input volumes via cp -a
+
+### [ ] Write tests for local input copy init containers
+- Test that when source node == current node, init container uses `cp -a` (not tar).
+- Test that the source path is the producing step's hostPath subdirectory.
+- Test that the dest path is this step's own hostPath subdirectory.
+- Test that inputs are writable after copy.
+- File: `atc/worker/jetbridge/daemonset_integration_test.go`
+
+### [ ] Implement cp -a init containers for local inputs
+- In `buildArtifactInitContainers()`, when DaemonSet mode + local:
+  - Source: `/var/concourse/artifacts/steps/<source-handle>/<name>/`
+  - Dest: `/var/concourse/artifacts/steps/<this-handle>/<input-name>/`
+  - Command: `cp -a <source>/. <dest>/`
+- When remote: HTTP GET from daemon, pipe to `tar xf - -C <dest>`.
+- Init container mounts the hostPath volume (parent directory) with read-write.
+- Files: `atc/worker/jetbridge/container.go`
+
+## Phase 4: Direct hostPath cache mounts
+
+### [ ] Write tests for direct cache hostPath mounts
+- Test that DaemonSet-mode caches are hostPath volumes with stable keys.
+- Test that cache path is `<hostPath>/caches/<stable-key>/`.
+- Test that no init container is created for cache restore.
+- Test that no upload is needed for cache save.
+- File: `atc/worker/jetbridge/daemonset_integration_test.go`
+
+### [ ] Implement direct cache hostPath mounts
+- In `buildVolumeMounts()`, add a new case for DaemonSet + cache:
+  - HostPath: `<ArtifactDaemonHostPath>/caches/<stableCacheKey>/`
+  - Type: `DirectoryOrCreate`
+  - No cacheEntry created (no tar save/restore needed).
+- Record cache location in `artifactLocator` for soft affinity.
+- Files: `atc/worker/jetbridge/container.go`
+
+## Phase 5: Build log events for fetch source
+
+### [ ] Write tests for fetch source log events
+- Test that the delegate emits a Log event per input indicating local vs remote.
+- Test that the node name is included for remote fetches.
+- Test that "location unknown" is emitted when locator has no record.
+- File: `atc/engine/task_delegate_test.go` or `atc/exec/task_step_test.go`
+
+### [ ] Implement fetch source log events
+- In the task step (or delegate), before container creation, emit a Log event per input:
+  - Local: `input "<name>": copying from local artifact cache`
+  - Remote: `input "<name>": fetching from node <node-name>`
+  - Unknown: `input "<name>": location unknown, will attempt local first`
+- Use the `ArtifactLocator` to determine source node.
+- The locator needs to be accessible from the step delegate or wired through the container spec.
+- Files: `atc/exec/task_step.go` or `atc/engine/task_delegate.go`
+
+## Phase 6: Reaper and GC updates
+
+### [ ] Write tests for directory-based reaper cleanup
+- Test that the reaper sends HTTP DELETE for the step directory (not a tar file).
+- Test that cache directories are not deleted by the reaper (only step directories).
+- Test that DB-driven cache GC removes cache hostPath directories.
+- File: `atc/worker/jetbridge/reaper_test.go`
+
+### [ ] Update reaper for directory-based cleanup
+- In `cleanupDaemonSetArtifacts()`, DELETE URL changes to `/artifacts/steps/<handle>/`.
+- Cache cleanup remains DB-driven: when cache volumes are "destroying", remove `/caches/<key>/`.
+- Files: `atc/worker/jetbridge/reaper.go`
+
+## Phase 7: DaemonSetVolume StreamOut for set_pipeline/load_var
+
+### [ ] Update DaemonSetVolume.StreamOut for directories
+- StreamOut HTTP GETs from the daemon, which now tars on-the-fly from the directory.
+- The response is the same tar stream, so StreamOut callers don't change.
+- Update the URL path to `/artifacts/steps/<handle>/<name>`.
+- File: `atc/worker/jetbridge/volume_daemonset.go`
+
+## Phase 8: Validation
+
+### [ ] Run the 4 previously-failing behavioral tests
+- Build image, deploy to KinD, run focused tests.
+- Verify all pass with the reworked DaemonSet mode.
+
+### [ ] Run jetbridge unit tests
+- `go test ./atc/worker/jetbridge/ -v -count=1`
+- `go test ./cmd/artifact-daemon/ -v -count=1`
+- Verify all existing + new tests pass.
